.TH BREW-OUTDATED-REPORT 1 "October 26, 2026" "homebrew-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
brew-outdated-report \- Markdown report of outdated Homebrew packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B brew-outdated-report
[\fB\-i\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-g\fR]
[\fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-title\fR \fITEXT\fR]
[\fB\-\-fail\-on\-outdated\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B brew-outdated-report
runs
.B brew outdated \-\-json=v2
with auto\-update disabled, or reads that JSON from a file, and writes a
Markdown report: a summary table, one table for formulae and one for casks,
and the exact upgrade commands.
.PP
Every change is classified as major, minor, patch, other or rebuild (a
Homebrew revision such as 1.7.1_1), and rows are sorted by that severity.
Pinned formulae are listed but left out of the upgrade command.
The tool never upgrades anything.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-input " " \fIFILE\fR
Read the JSON from \fIFILE\fR, or from standard input when \fIFILE\fR is \-.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-greedy
Include casks that update themselves.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Write the report to \fIFILE\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-title " TEXT"
Title of the report.
.TP
.B \-\-fail\-on\-outdated
Exit 1 when anything is outdated.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
When set, fixes the report timestamp, so the same input gives the same bytes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Report written.
.TP
.B 1
Report written and something is outdated, with \-\-fail\-on\-outdated.
.TP
.B 64
Usage error.
.TP
.B 65
The input is not brew outdated \-\-json=v2 output.
.TP
.B 69
jq or brew is not available.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
brew\-outdated\-report > outdated.md
brew\-outdated\-report \-\-greedy \-\-output ~/Desktop/brew.md
brew outdated \-\-json=v2 | brew\-outdated\-report \-\-input \-
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR brew (1),
.BR jq (1)
